cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Planck in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Planck: A quantum chemistry program for Hartree-Fock and Kohn-Sham DFT"
abstract: >-
Planck is a quantum chemistry program implementing Hartree-Fock (RHF/UHF/ROHF) and Kohn-Sham density functional theory (RKS/UKS), with MP2, coupled cluster (RCCSD/UCCSD through RCCSDTQ and arbitrary-order RCC via generated residuals), CASSCF/SA-CASSCF/RASSCF, FCI, TDDFT, analytic gradients, geometry optimization in redundant internal coordinates, semi-numerical frequencies, PCM solvation, ghost-atom counterpoise corrections, and full point-group symmetry reduction of the ERI tensor in both Cartesian and spherical-harmonic bases.
